meta {
  name: Print Order Document
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/print
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "bill_print",
    "templateId": "{{pdfReportTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Render one of the order's documents to a PDF using the selected
  `PdfReportTemplate`, streamed back as `application/pdf` (raw binary — NOT the
  JSON envelope). The backend builds the render context from the order's real
  data (patient, items, referral, payment ledger) and interpolates the template's
  `{mustache}` placeholders + `{{#each}}` sections.

  ## Body
  - `type` (required) — which order document to render. One of:
    - `order_print` — the order slip (header, patient, referral, item list).
    - `bill_print` — the patient bill (amounts + item list + payment history).
    - `accounts_biling` — the accounts / B2B billing document (bill context + the
      referral panel's accounts-person contact block). Used as the attachment for
      the Billings "Share and Inform" flow.
    - `trf_print` — the Test Requisition Form (requested tests + clinical notes).
    - `lab_quotation_print` — the quotation (items + totals + validity).
    - `order_barcode_print` — a barcode label for the order's own identifier
      (`orderCode`) plus a short patient/test summary. Distinct from
      `order_label_print`, which is the per-`AccessionSample` specimen barcode
      printed via `POST /accession/order-samples/print-label(s)` — this type is for
      the Order Console's per-row "Print Order Barcode" action, not specimen
      tracking.
  - `templateId` (optional) — the `PdfReportTemplate` to render with. The frontend
    picker always sends the selected id. Omit to fall back to the tenant's single
    active template of `type`.

  ## Errors
  - 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` — order missing / soft-deleted / other tenant.
  - 404 `NO_ACTIVE_ORDER_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — no active template of `type` and no
    explicit `templateId`.
  - 409 `AMBIGUOUS_ORDER_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — several active templates of `type` and
    no `templateId` supplied.
  - 409 `BILL_COPY_PRINT_NOT_ALLOWED_FOR_UNPAID` — a **bill document**
    (`bill_print`, `accounts_biling`, or `referral_patient_bill_print`) while the
    branch Registration Setting
    `BillingMenu_AllowBillCopyPrintForPaidBillingsOnly` is on and the order's
    billing `status !== PAID`. The gate is keyed on the derived bill status
    (cancellation + refunds folded in) — so Cancelled / Require-Refund / Partially-
    or Fully-Refunded / unpaid orders are all blocked, exactly matching the
    Billings "Paid" badge and the Share Bill gate. `trf_print`, `order_print`,
    `lab_quotation_print`, and `order_barcode_print` are never gated.

  ## Bill amount tags (bill_print / accounts_biling / referral_patient_bill_print)

  The bill context exposes the authoritative rollups (the SAME values the Billings
  list and View Bill show — `computeBillingTotals`, not a raw ledger sum):
  `gross_amount`, `discount_amount`, `net_amount`, `paid_amount`, and a
  refund-aware `balance_amount` (net − effective-paid). It also exposes
  `refund_total`, `refund_charge_total`, `cancellation_charge`, and `effective_paid`
  so the bill can show money returned and retained fees. Each `sections.payments`
  row carries `type` (`Payment`/`Refund`), `amount` (paid for a Payment, refunded
  for a Refund — a refund no longer prints as ₹0), `mode`, `reference`,
  `refund_charge`. The seeded default `bill_print`/`accounts_biling` templates were
  updated to render these; existing tenant templates can adopt the new tags via the
  Old Templates editor.

  In Bruno, use "Save Response → Save to file" to inspect the PDF.
}
